      "totalDuration": "10 yrs 10 mos",
      "description": "Developed data plane drivers and diagnostic software for latest generation of Quantum Flow Processor (QFP) in Cisco’s ASR1000 line of routers\n• Collaborated with ASIC team to debug complex performance issues\n• Extended and implemented production and diagnostic software for next gen QFP hardware\n• Prime tensilica contact for compiler related issues, reduced remote site build time by 2 hours\n• Designed and implemented Serial Atris packet buffer memory derisk software to verify and qualify memory parts\n• Extended diagnostic TCAM memory stress tests to support new Serial TCAM design (including support for multiple vendors)\n• Created common SerDes infrastructure to support interface testing including PRBS and eye scan capabilities\n• Added support for completely new BQS (scheduling hardware) design into the diagnostic traffic tests\n• Mentored and brought up to speed new team members and interns\n• SELinux compliance for data plane processes",
      "insights": ""
     },
     {
      "title": "Software Engineer",
      "timePeriod": {
       "startDate": {
        "year": 2014
       },
       "endDate": {
        "year": 2016
       }
      },
      "totalDuration": "2 yrs",
      "description": "Key Data Plane team member responsible for adding QFP (2nd gen) support for ASR1001-HX and ASR1002-HX enterprise routers\n• From bringing the board up in lab to seeing it sold on cisco.com, made sure the dataplane met and exceeded product requirements\n• Verified aggregate bandwidth and basic feature testing using Ixia packet generators (NDR, QOS, basic routing, end-to-end flow control)\n• Took part in ISO audit for the ASR-HX program\n• Worked across multiple teams and timezones to make sure requirements were met in a timely fashion\n• Managed lab testbed which included setting up reservation system, configuring and cabling network to meet team's needs",
      "insights": ""
     },
     {
      "title": "Software Engineer",
      "timePeriod": {
       "startDate": {
        "month": 6,
